@page "/features"

<PageTitle>Features | One Big Team</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Explore One Big Team features for employee management, leave, absence, recruitment, documents, workflows, reminders and reporting.">
</HeadContent>

<SiteHeader CurrentPage="features" />

<main>
  <section class="features-hero section-band">
    <div class="section-inner two-column">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Features</p>
        <h1>One simple platform for everyday HR admin.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="copy-block">
        <p class="hero-text">
          One Big Team helps growing businesses replace spreadsheets, email trails
          and disconnected HR admin with one simple platform for people, documents,
          hiring, absence and reporting.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions" id="trial">
          <a class="button button-primary button-large" href="/contact#contact-form">Start free trial</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary button-large" href="/pricing">View pricing</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section feature-index-section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Product areas</p>
        <h2>Everything is designed to keep growing teams organised.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-index">
        <a href="#employee-management">Employee management</a>
        <a href="#leave-management">Leave management</a>
        <a href="#sickness-absence">Sickness and absence</a>
        <a href="#recruitment">Recruitment</a>
        <a href="#company-documents">Company documents</a>
        <a href="#workflows-reminders">Workflows and reminders</a>
        <a href="#reporting">Reporting</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="employee-management" class="section section-muted feature-detail-section">
    <div class="section-inner feature-detail">
      <div>
        <span class="feature-kicker">01</span>
        <h2>Employee management</h2>
        <p>
          Keep core employee information organised, accessible and consistent as your
          business grows beyond ad hoc files and scattered records.
        </p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#trial">Start free trial</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="feature-benefits">
        <li>Centralise employee profiles, roles and key employment details.</li>
        <li>Give managers a clearer view of the people they support.</li>
        <li>Reduce duplicate records across spreadsheets and shared drives.</li>
        <li>Make everyday HR information easier to find when decisions are needed.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="leave-management" class="section feature-detail-section">
    <div class="section-inner feature-detail">
      <div>
        <span class="feature-kicker">02</span>
        <h2>Leave management</h2>
        <p>
          Bring leave requests, balances and approvals into a shared process so
          everyone understands who is away and what needs action.
        </p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#trial">Start free trial</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="feature-benefits">
        <li>Replace back-and-forth email requests with a clearer approval path.</li>
        <li>Help managers plan cover with better visibility of upcoming leave.</li>
        <li>Keep absence records in the same system as employee information.</li>
        <li>Support consistent leave handling across teams and locations.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="sickness-absence" class="section section-muted feature-detail-section">
    <div class="section-inner feature-detail">
      <div>
        <span class="feature-kicker">03</span>
        <h2>Sickness and absence</h2>
        <p>
          Track sickness and other absence clearly, so managers can respond with
          better context and keep records complete without relying on inbox history.
        </p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#trial">Start free trial</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="feature-benefits">
        <li>Record sickness events consistently across the organisation.</li>
        <li>Keep absence context close to the employee record.</li>
        <li>Spot patterns that may need follow-up or manager support.</li>
        <li>Reduce reliance on informal notes and fragmented email trails.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="recruitment" class="section feature-detail-section">
    <div class="section-inner feature-detail">
      <div>
        <span class="feature-kicker">04</span>
        <h2>Recruitment</h2>
        <p>
          Give hiring activity a simple home, from open roles to candidate progress,
          so recruitment does not disappear into personal inboxes.
        </p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#trial">Start free trial</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="feature-benefits">
        <li>Track roles, candidates and hiring stages in one place.</li>
        <li>Help hiring managers understand what needs attention next.</li>
        <li>Keep recruitment notes easier to share with the right people.</li>
        <li>Improve continuity when hiring involves multiple team members.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="company-documents" class="section section-muted feature-detail-section">
    <div class="section-inner feature-detail">
      <div>
        <span class="feature-kicker">05</span>
        <h2>Company documents</h2>
        <p>
          Store company policies, templates and employee-facing documents where
          teams can find the right version without searching several folders.
        </p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#trial">Start free trial</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="feature-benefits">
        <li>Keep key HR documents in an organised shared library.</li>
        <li>Make policies and templates easier for employees to access.</li>
        <li>Reduce confusion caused by outdated copies in different locations.</li>
        <li>Support clearer onboarding and internal communication.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="workflows-reminders" class="section feature-detail-section">
    <div class="section-inner feature-detail">
      <div>
        <span class="feature-kicker">06</span>
        <h2>Workflows and reminders</h2>
        <p>
          Turn repeat HR admin into more reliable prompts and follow-ups, helping
          managers stay on top of tasks that otherwise depend on memory.
        </p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#trial">Start free trial</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="feature-benefits">
        <li>Give recurring HR tasks a clearer route from request to completion.</li>
        <li>Prompt the right people when reviews, checks or follow-ups are due.</li>
        <li>Reduce manual chasing for routine people operations.</li>
        <li>Help growing teams keep processes consistent as headcount increases.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="reporting" class="section section-muted feature-detail-section">
    <div class="section-inner feature-detail">
      <div>
        <span class="feature-kicker">07</span>
        <h2>Reporting</h2>
        <p>
          See useful people information more clearly, so leaders can understand
          workforce activity without stitching together separate spreadsheets.
        </p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="#trial">Start free trial</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="feature-benefits">
        <li>Understand headcount, absence, leave and hiring activity at a glance.</li>
        <li>Give managers better context for planning and follow-up.</li>
        <li>Reduce time spent preparing manual status updates.</li>
        <li>Support more confident people decisions as the business grows.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="section final-cta">
    <div class="section-inner cta-panel">
      <p class="eyebrow">Ready to replace scattered HR admin?</p>
      <h2>Start building one simple people workspace for your growing team.</h2>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary button-large" href="/contact#contact-form">Start free trial</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary button-large" href="/contact#contact-form">Contact us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<SiteFooter />
